<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="viewing-logs-api">
  <title>Viewing detailed logs</title>
  <shortdesc>To inspect individual registry events for a user, organization, or repository in Red Hat Quay, you can retrieve detailed logs through the API. You can filter results by performer and date range.</shortdesc>
  <taskbody>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>GET /api/v1/user/logs</codeph> API endpoint to return a list of log entries for a user. For example:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X GET   -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;bearer_token&gt;"   -H "Accept: application/json"   "&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/user/logs"</codeblock>
          <p>You can also pass in the <codeph>performer</codeph> and <codeph>starttime/endtime</codeph> queries to obtain logs for a specific user between a specific time period. For example:</p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X GET   -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;bearer_token&gt;"   -H "Accept: application/json"   "http://quay-server.example.com/api/v1/user/logs?performer=quayuser&amp;starttime=01/01/2024&amp;endtime=06/18/2024"</codeblock>
          <p>The following example shows detailed log output:</p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">---
{"start_time": "Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 -0000", "end_time": "Wed, 19 Jun 2024 00:00:00 -0000", "logs": [{"kind": "revert_tag", "metadata": {"username": "quayuser", "repo": "busybox", "tag": "test-two", "manifest_digest": "sha256:57583a1b9c0a7509d3417387b4f43acf80d08cdcf5266ac87987be3f8f919d5d"}, "ip": "192.168.1.131", "datetime": "Tue, 18 Jun 2024 18:59:13 -0000", "performer": {"kind": "user", "name": "quayuser", "is_robot": false, "avatar": {"name": "quayuser", "hash": "b28d563a6dc76b4431fc7b0524bbff6b810387dac86d9303874871839859c7cc", "color": "#17becf", "kind": "user"}}}, {"kind": "push_repo", "metadata": {"repo": "busybox", "namespace": "quayuser", "user-agent": "containers/5.30.1 (github.com/containers/image)", "tag": "test-two", "username": "quayuser", }
---</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>GET /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/logs</codeph> endpoint to return logs for a specified organization:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;bearer_token&gt;" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  "http://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/organization/{orgname}/logs"</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>GET /api/v1/repository/{repository}/logs</codeph> endpoint to return logs for a specified repository:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;bearer_token&gt;" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  "http://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/repository/{repository}/logs"</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
    </steps>
  </taskbody>
</task>
